Subject: [PATCH] spi: airoha-snfi: check SFC strap on EcoNet EN7528 as well

The EN7528 (econet target) uses the same SNFI controller as EN7523/EN7581
("identical register layouts", see 303-spi-airoha-snfi-enable-for-econet).
The RESERVED-mode strap check (UART_TXD shorted to GND -> known incorrect
DMA reading of some flashes) was gated on the EN7523 compatible string
only, so on EN7528 boards the driver always used DMA even when the strap
indicates the reserved mode.

Extend the check to the EN7581/EN7528 compatible string and always print
the raw strap value, so a failing flash probe can be diagnosed from the
boot log:

    airoha-snand 1fa10000.spi: SFC strap: 0x????????   <- bit2=0 => reserved mode

Behaviour is unchanged when the strap bit is set (normal mode); in reserved
mode the driver falls back to the slower but correct PIO path.

Signed-off-by: ZCode <zcode@local>
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c
@@ -1099,10 +1099,13 @@ static int airoha_snand_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(as_ctrl->spi_clk),
 				     "unable to get spi clk\n");
 
-	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,en7523-snand")) {
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,en7523-snand") ||
+	    device_is_compatible(dev, "airoha,en7581-snand")) {
 		err = regmap_read(as_ctrl->regmap_ctrl,
 				  REG_SPI_CTRL_SFC_STRAP, &sfc_strap);
 		if (err)
 			return err;
 
+		dev_info(dev, "SFC strap: 0x%08x\n", sfc_strap);
+
 		if (!(sfc_strap & 0x04)) {
 			dma_enable = false;
 			dev_warn(dev, "Detected booting in RESERVED mode (UART_TXD was short to GND).\n");
